IMPORT prelude

-- Spam Control Act 2007 (Singapore) -- Parts 1, 2 and 3, and both Schedules.
--
-- The Act creates no offence. It creates two prohibitions (s 9, s 11), a
-- prohibition on helping to breach them (s 12), and a private right of action
-- for a person who suffers loss (s 13). This file carries the definitions that
-- decide whether the prohibitions bite, and the Second Schedule requirements
-- that s 11 imports. Part 4 is in spam-civil-action.l4.
--
-- Edition: 2020 Revised Edition, informal consolidation in force from
-- 1 April 2022, as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/SCA2007.txt
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules
-- skill. No pipeline, no coverage table, no independent test pass, no human
-- gate.
--
-- NOT ENCODED: s 1 (short title), s 16 (codes of practice -- a power to issue
-- and a duty to comply with whatever is issued; the codes themselves were not
-- retrieved), s 17 (amendment of Schedules) and s 18 (regulations). Each
-- confers a power and decides nothing on its own.

§ `Spam Control Act 2007 -- definitions and the two prohibitions`

§§ `2 -- electronic address, and the three kinds there are`

-- s 2: "'electronic address' means an email address, an instant messaging
-- account or a mobile telephone number to which an electronic message can be
-- sent".
--
-- The kind matters three times over, and differently each time:
--   s 8(2)  excludes a mobile telephone number from Part 2;
--   s 4A    says a message to an instant messaging account is not a message to
--           the email address or mobile number that names the account;
--   Second Schedule para 3(3) excludes an instant messaging account from the
--           labelling requirements.
DECLARE AddressKind IS ONE OF
    `an email address`
    `an instant messaging account`
    `a mobile telephone number`

§§ `3 -- the primary purpose of a commercial electronic message`

-- s 3(1): a message is commercial where, having regard to its content, its
-- presentation and the content reachable through its links, numbers or contact
-- information, "it is concluded that the primary purpose of the message is" one
-- of twelve things, paragraphs (d) to (o).
--
-- The conclusion itself is a judgment on the whole message and is a FACT
-- SUPPLIED here: this encoding takes the primary purpose as given and decides
-- only whether that purpose is one the section names.
DECLARE PrimaryPurpose IS ONE OF
    `to offer to supply goods or services`
    `to advertise or promote goods or services`
    `to advertise or promote a supplier of goods or services`
    `to offer to supply land or an interest in land`
    `to advertise or promote land or an interest in land`
    `to advertise or promote a supplier of land`
    `to offer to provide a business or investment opportunity`
    `to advertise or promote a business or investment opportunity`
    `to advertise or promote a provider of such an opportunity`
    `to assist a person by deception to dishonestly obtain property`
    `to assist a person by deception to dishonestly obtain a financial advantage`
    `to assist a person to dishonestly obtain a gain`
    `something the section does not name`

GIVEN `the primary purpose` IS A PrimaryPurpose
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the primary purpose is one named in section 3(1)` IF
    CONSIDER `the primary purpose`
    WHEN `something the section does not name` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

-- s 3(2): "For the purposes of PARAGRAPHS (d) TO (l) of subsection (1), it does
-- not matter -- (a) whether the goods, services, land, interest or opportunity
-- exists; or (b) whether it is lawful to acquire" it.
--
-- The subsection is confined to (d) to (l). It says nothing about the three
-- deception limbs (m), (n) and (o), which is unsurprising -- the thing a fraud
-- offers never exists -- but it means the deeming is not available there.
GIVEN `the primary purpose` IS A PrimaryPurpose
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `section 3(2) makes existence and lawfulness irrelevant` IF
    CONSIDER `the primary purpose`
    WHEN `to assist a person by deception to dishonestly obtain property` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `to assist a person by deception to dishonestly obtain a financial advantage` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `to assist a person to dishonestly obtain a gain` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `something the section does not name` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

§§ `2, 3(4), 3(5) -- who is the sender`

-- s 2: "'sender', in relation to an electronic message, means a person who
-- sends the message, causes the message to be sent, or authorises the sending
-- of the message".
--
-- s 3(4): a person "who KNOWINGLY ALLOWS the person's product or service to be
-- advertised or promoted by a sender is DEEMED to have authorised the sending".
-- s 3(5): but a person "who takes REASONABLE STEPS to stop the sending" of such
-- a message "is deemed NOT to have authorised the sending".
--
-- So the advertiser whose product is being promoted is a sender by deeming, and
-- gets out only by taking reasonable steps. Doing nothing is not enough; and
-- s 3(5) does not require the steps to have worked.
DECLARE PersonsPart HAS
    `sent the message` IS A BOOLEAN
    `caused the message to be sent` IS A BOOLEAN
    `authorised the sending of the message` IS A BOOLEAN
    `knowingly allowed their product to be advertised or promoted by a sender` IS A BOOLEAN
    `took reasonable steps to stop the sending` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the part` IS A PersonsPart
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the person is deemed by section 3(4) to have authorised the sending` IF
        `the part`'s `knowingly allowed their product to be advertised or promoted by a sender`
    AND NOT `the part`'s `took reasonable steps to stop the sending`

GIVEN `the part` IS A PersonsPart
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the person is the sender of the message` IF
        `the part`'s `sent the message`
    OR  `the part`'s `caused the message to be sent`
    OR  `the part`'s `authorised the sending of the message`
    OR  `the person is deemed by section 3(4) to have authorised the sending` `the part`

§§ `4 and 4A -- what an electronic message is, and what address it was sent to`

-- s 4(1): "an electronic message is a message sent to an electronic address".
-- s 4(2): it does not matter "(a) whether the electronic address exists; or
--   (b) whether the message reaches its intended destination."
-- s 4(3): "a message is NOT an electronic message if it is sent by way of a
--   voice call made using a telephone service."
--
-- s 4(2) has no operative content of its own. It is encoded as two fields that
-- nothing reads, and the cases file asserts that varying them changes no
-- answer. That is the whole of what the subsection does.
DECLARE Message HAS
    `the kind of address it was sent to` IS AN AddressKind
    `the instant messaging account is named by an email address or a mobile number` IS A BOOLEAN
    `sent by way of a voice call made using a telephone service` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the electronic address exists` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the message reached its intended destination` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the primary purpose` IS A PrimaryPurpose
    `the recipient requested to receive the message` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the recipient consented to the receipt of the message` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the only ground for that request or consent is that the address was given or published by the recipient` IS A BOOLEAN
    `sent more than 10 business days after the recipient submitted an unsubscribe request` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the message` IS A Message
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the message is an electronic message` IF
    NOT `the message`'s `sent by way of a voice call made using a telephone service`

-- s 4A: "where an electronic message is sent to an instant messaging account;
-- and the name used to identify, or which is associated with, that instant
-- messaging account is an email address or a mobile telephone number, the
-- electronic message is NOT a message sent to the email address or mobile
-- telephone number".
--
-- This is the provision that keeps a messaging-app blast out of the
-- mobile-number carve-outs, and it is the reason the next function is not
-- simply a field read.
GIVEN `the message` IS A Message
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the message is sent to a mobile telephone number for the purposes of this Act` IF
    CONSIDER `the message`'s `the kind of address it was sent to`
    WHEN `a mobile telephone number` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `an instant messaging account` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

GIVEN `the message` IS A Message
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the message is sent to an email address for the purposes of this Act` IF
    CONSIDER `the message`'s `the kind of address it was sent to`
    WHEN `an email address` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `an instant messaging account` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

§§ `5 -- unsolicited`

-- s 5(1): a message is unsolicited "if the recipient did not -- (a) request to
--   receive the message; or (b) consent to the receipt of the message."
-- s 5(2): a recipient is not treated as having requested or consented "MERELY
--   BECAUSE the electronic address of the recipient was given or published by or
--   on behalf of the recipient."
-- s 5(3): where a recipient of a message "OTHER THAN an unsolicited electronic
--   message" submits an unsubscribe request, the recipient is not treated as
--   having requested or consented to any message sent after the expiry of
--   10 business days after the day the request was submitted.
--
-- s 5(3) is the one that turns a lawful mailing list into an unlawful one. Note
-- its opening words: it operates on a recipient of a message that was NOT
-- unsolicited -- that is, on someone who had subscribed. It is the withdrawal
-- of a consent that existed.
GIVEN `the message` IS A Message
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the recipient is treated as having requested or consented` IF
         (    `the message`'s `the recipient requested to receive the message`
          OR  `the message`'s `the recipient consented to the receipt of the message`)
    AND NOT `the message`'s `the only ground for that request or consent is that the address was given or published by the recipient`
    AND NOT `the message`'s `sent more than 10 business days after the recipient submitted an unsubscribe request`

GIVEN `the message` IS A Message
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the message is unsolicited` IF
    NOT `the recipient is treated as having requested or consented` `the message`

GIVEN `the message` IS A Message
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the message is a commercial electronic message` IF
        `the message is an electronic message` `the message`
    AND `the primary purpose is one named in section 3(1)` (`the message`'s `the primary purpose`)

GIVEN `the message` IS A Message
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the message is an unsolicited commercial electronic message` IF
        `the message is a commercial electronic message` `the message`
    AND `the message is unsolicited` `the message`

§§ `6 -- sending in bulk`

-- s 6(1): messages are "DEEMED to be sent in bulk" if a person sends, causes to
-- be sent or authorises the sending of --
--   (a) more than 100 messages of the same or similar subject matter in 24 hours;
--   (b) more than 1,000 in a 30-day period; or
--   (c) more than 10,000 in a one-year period.
-- s 6(2): the Minister may vary any of the three numbers by order in the Gazette.
--
-- The three are alternatives, and the first is by far the tightest: 100 a day
-- sustained for a month is 3,000, which clears limb (b) three times over. A
-- sender who wants to stay outside the Act must satisfy all three at once.
--
-- The thresholds are carried as parameters rather than written in, because
-- s 6(2) lets the Minister change them. The cases file supplies the figures the
-- Act itself states.
DECLARE SendingVolume HAS
    `messages of similar subject matter sent during a 24-hour period` IS A NUMBER
    `messages of similar subject matter sent during a 30-day period` IS A NUMBER
    `messages of similar subject matter sent during a one-year period` IS A NUMBER

DECLARE BulkThresholds HAS
    `the 24-hour threshold` IS A NUMBER
    `the 30-day threshold` IS A NUMBER
    `the one-year threshold` IS A NUMBER

`the thresholds in section 6(1) as enacted` MEANS BulkThresholds WITH
    `the 24-hour threshold` IS 100
    `the 30-day threshold` IS 1000
    `the one-year threshold` IS 10000

GIVEN `the volume` IS A SendingVolume, `the thresholds` IS A BulkThresholds
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the messages are deemed to be sent in bulk` IF
        `the volume`'s `messages of similar subject matter sent during a 24-hour period`
            GREATER THAN `the thresholds`'s `the 24-hour threshold`
    OR  `the volume`'s `messages of similar subject matter sent during a 30-day period`
            GREATER THAN `the thresholds`'s `the 30-day threshold`
    OR  `the volume`'s `messages of similar subject matter sent during a one-year period`
            GREATER THAN `the thresholds`'s `the one-year threshold`

§§ `7 and the First Schedule -- when the Act applies at all`

-- s 7(1): "This Act does not apply unless an electronic message has a Singapore
-- link." s 7(2) lists five circumstances in which it has one. Any one is enough.
--
-- Limb (e) is a counterfactual: where the message could not be delivered
-- because the address no longer exists, the link is established if it is
-- "reasonably likely that the message WOULD HAVE BEEN accessed using a
-- computer, mobile telephone, server or device located in Singapore". That is
-- the subsection that makes s 4(2)(b) -- it does not matter whether the message
-- arrives -- do any work.
DECLARE SingaporeLink HAS
    `the message originates in Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the sender is an individual physically present in Singapore when the message is sent` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the sender is an entity formed or recognised under the law of Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the sender is an entity with an office or place of business in Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the device used to access the message is located in Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the recipient is an individual physically present in Singapore when the message is accessed` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the recipient is an entity carrying on business in Singapore when the message is accessed` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the message could not be delivered and would likely have been accessed on a device in Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the link` IS A SingaporeLink
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the message has a Singapore link` IF
        `the link`'s `the message originates in Singapore`
    OR  `the link`'s `the sender is an individual physically present in Singapore when the message is sent`
    OR  `the link`'s `the sender is an entity formed or recognised under the law of Singapore`
    OR  `the link`'s `the sender is an entity with an office or place of business in Singapore`
    OR  `the link`'s `the device used to access the message is located in Singapore`
    OR  `the link`'s `the recipient is an individual physically present in Singapore when the message is accessed`
    OR  `the link`'s `the recipient is an entity carrying on business in Singapore when the message is accessed`
    OR  `the link`'s `the message could not be delivered and would likely have been accessed on a device in Singapore`

-- s 7(3) and First Schedule para 1: the Act does not apply to a message "where
-- the sending of the message is authorised by the Government or a statutory body
-- on the occurrence of any public emergency, in the public interest or in the
-- interests of public security or national defence."
--
-- First Schedule para 2: where doubt arises about the emergency or about public
-- security or national defence, "a certificate signed by the Minister is
-- CONCLUSIVE EVIDENCE of the matters stated in the certificate." Note what the
-- certificate route covers: the emergency limb and the security limb. A doubt
-- about whether sending was "in the public interest" -- the widest of the three
-- -- has no certificate and no stated way of being settled.
DECLARE Authorisation HAS
    `the sending is authorised by the Government or a statutory body` IS A BOOLEAN
    `on the occurrence of a public emergency` IS A BOOLEAN
    `in the public interest` IS A BOOLEAN
    `in the interests of public security or national defence` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the authorisation` IS AN Authorisation
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the message is excluded by the First Schedule` IF
        `the authorisation`'s `the sending is authorised by the Government or a statutory body`
    AND (    `the authorisation`'s `on the occurrence of a public emergency`
         OR  `the authorisation`'s `in the public interest`
         OR  `the authorisation`'s `in the interests of public security or national defence`)

-- First Schedule para 2 settles two of the three limbs conclusively.
GIVEN `the authorisation` IS AN Authorisation
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a ministerial certificate can settle the doubt` IF
        `the authorisation`'s `on the occurrence of a public emergency`
    OR  `the authorisation`'s `in the interests of public security or national defence`

GIVEN `the message` IS A Message,
      `the link` IS A SingaporeLink,
      `the authorisation` IS AN Authorisation
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `this Act applies to the message` IF
        `the message has a Singapore link` `the link`
    AND NOT `the message is excluded by the First Schedule` `the authorisation`

§§ `8 and 9 -- dictionary attack and address-harvesting software`

-- s 9: "A person must not send, cause to be sent, or authorise the sending of,
-- an electronic message to electronic addresses generated or obtained through
-- the use of -- (a) a dictionary attack; or (b) address-harvesting software."
--
-- s 8(1): this Part applies to ALL electronic messages, "whether or not they are
-- unsolicited commercial electronic messages".
-- s 8(2): "This Part does NOT apply to any electronic message sent to a MOBILE
-- TELEPHONE NUMBER."
--
-- The exclusion in s 8(2) is the largest hole in the Act, and it is worth
-- stating plainly: the long title describes an Act about spam "sent in bulk by
-- email or by text or multimedia messaging to mobile telephone numbers", and
-- Part 2 then declines to apply to mobile telephone numbers at all. A person who
-- generates mobile numbers by permutation and texts every one of them does not
-- contravene s 9. They may still contravene s 11 -- but only if the messages are
-- unsolicited, commercial and in bulk, and s 11 asks for a compliant unsubscribe
-- facility and an <ADV> label, not for the numbers to have been honestly got.
--
-- s 4A matters here: a message to an instant messaging account named by a mobile
-- number is not a message sent to that mobile number, so s 8(2) leaves it inside
-- Part 2.
GIVEN `the message` IS A Message
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Part 2 applies to the message` IF
        `the message is an electronic message` `the message`
    AND NOT `the message is sent to a mobile telephone number for the purposes of this Act` `the message`

DECLARE HowTheAddressesWereObtained IS ONE OF
    `through the use of a dictionary attack`
    `through the use of address-harvesting software`
    `otherwise`

GIVEN `how the addresses were obtained` IS A HowTheAddressesWereObtained
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the addresses were obtained by a means section 9 names` IF
    CONSIDER `how the addresses were obtained`
    WHEN `otherwise` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

GIVEN `the message` IS A Message,
      `the part` IS A PersonsPart,
      `how the addresses were obtained` IS A HowTheAddressesWereObtained
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the person contravenes section 9` IF
        `Part 2 applies to the message` `the message`
    AND `the person is the sender of the message` `the part`
    AND `the addresses were obtained by a means section 9 names` `how the addresses were obtained`

§§ `10, 11 and the Second Schedule -- the requirements for bulk spam`

-- s 10: "This Part applies ONLY to unsolicited commercial electronic messages."
-- s 11: "Any person who sends, causes to be sent or authorises the sending of
-- unsolicited commercial electronic messages IN BULK must comply with the
-- requirements in the Second Schedule."
--
-- The Second Schedule opens each requirement with "EVERY unsolicited commercial
-- electronic message must contain ...". s 11 imports it only for a person
-- sending in bulk. So the Schedule on its face binds every unsolicited
-- commercial message, and the section that gives it force binds only bulk
-- senders. Nothing else in the Act picks the Schedule up: s 17 lets the Minister
-- amend it, and s 13 gives a right of action for contravention of s 9 or s 11
-- and of nothing else. A single unsolicited commercial message with a false
-- subject line and no unsubscribe address therefore contravenes nothing.
--
-- This encoding follows s 11, not the Schedule's own wording. The function that
-- decides a contravention asks for bulk; the function that decides whether a
-- message meets the Schedule does not, so the two can be read apart and the
-- gap between them can be asserted.

§§§ `Second Schedule paragraph 2 -- the unsubscribe facility`

-- para 2(1): every message must contain (a) an email address, Internet location
--   address, telephone number, fax number or postal address the recipient may
--   use to submit an unsubscribe request, and (b) a statement to that effect.
-- para 2(2): where received BY EMAIL, it must include an EMAIL address for the
--   request.
-- para 2(3): where received by text or multimedia messaging to a mobile number,
--   it must include a mobile telephone number -- by text if received by text,
--   and by text or multimedia messaging at the recipient's option if received by
--   multimedia messaging.
-- para 2(4): the statement must be clear and conspicuous, and in English (and
--   where in two or more languages, English must be one of them).
-- para 2(5): the address or number must be (a) valid and capable of receiving
--   the request and a reasonable number of similar requests from others, "at all
--   times during a period of AT LEAST 30 DAYS after the message is sent", and
--   (b) legitimately obtained.
-- para 2(6): using it must not cost more than the usual cost of that kind of
--   address or number on the same kind of technology.
-- para 2(7): where a request is submitted using the facility, "no further
--   unsolicited commercial electronic messages may be sent after the expiry of
--   10 business days after the day on which the unsubscribe request is
--   submitted."
-- para 2(8): a person who receives a request must not disclose any information in
--   it without the consent of the person whose particulars it contains.
-- para 2(9): "SUB-PARAGRAPHS (1) TO (7) do not apply if the message is sent,
--   caused to be sent or authorised to be sent BY MISTAKE."
--
-- Note what 2(9) leaves standing. It lifts (1) to (7) for a mistaken message but
-- not 2(8): the duty not to disclose what is in an unsubscribe request survives,
-- which is right, since a mistaken mailing can still draw real requests.
--
-- "mistake" is defined in para 1 as "reasonable mistake of fact" -- not mistake
-- of law, and not an unreasonable one.
DECLARE UnsubscribeFacility HAS
    `contains an address or number for submitting an unsubscribe request` IS A BOOLEAN
    `contains a statement to the effect that it may be so used` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the address provided is an email address` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the number provided is a mobile number accepting a text request` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the number provided also accepts a multimedia request at the recipient's option` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the statement is presented in a clear and conspicuous manner` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the statement is presented in English or in English among other languages` IS A BOOLEAN
    `valid and capable of receiving the request and similar requests for at least 30 days` IS A BOOLEAN
    `legitimately obtained` IS A BOOLEAN
    `using it costs no more than the usual cost of that kind of address or number` IS A BOOLEAN
    `no further unsolicited commercial message was sent after 10 business days from the request` IS A BOOLEAN

DECLARE HowItWasReceived IS ONE OF
    `by email`
    `by text messaging to a mobile telephone number`
    `by multimedia messaging to a mobile telephone number`
    `at an instant messaging account`

-- 2(2) and 2(3) add a requirement on top of 2(1), and which one depends on how
-- the recipient received the message. A message received at an instant messaging
-- account attracts neither: 2(1) applies to it, but nothing says what kind of
-- return address it must carry.
GIVEN `the facility` IS AN UnsubscribeFacility, `how it was received` IS A HowItWasReceived
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the channel-specific requirement is met` IF
    CONSIDER `how it was received`
    WHEN `by email`
        THEN `the facility`'s `the address provided is an email address`
    WHEN `by text messaging to a mobile telephone number`
        THEN `the facility`'s `the number provided is a mobile number accepting a text request`
    WHEN `by multimedia messaging to a mobile telephone number`
        THEN     `the facility`'s `the number provided is a mobile number accepting a text request`
             AND `the facility`'s `the number provided also accepts a multimedia request at the recipient's option`
    OTHERWISE TRUE

GIVEN `the facility` IS AN UnsubscribeFacility,
      `how it was received` IS A HowItWasReceived,
      `sent by mistake` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `paragraph 2 is complied with` IF
        `sent by mistake`
    OR  (    `the facility`'s `contains an address or number for submitting an unsubscribe request`
         AND `the facility`'s `contains a statement to the effect that it may be so used`
         AND `the channel-specific requirement is met` `the facility` `how it was received`
         AND `the facility`'s `the statement is presented in a clear and conspicuous manner`
         AND `the facility`'s `the statement is presented in English or in English among other languages`
         AND `the facility`'s `valid and capable of receiving the request and similar requests for at least 30 days`
         AND `the facility`'s `legitimately obtained`
         AND `the facility`'s `using it costs no more than the usual cost of that kind of address or number`
         AND `the facility`'s `no further unsolicited commercial message was sent after 10 business days from the request`)

-- 2(8) stands on its own and survives a mistake.
GIVEN `disclosed what was in an unsubscribe request to another person` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `with the consent of the person whose particulars it contains` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `paragraph 2(8) is contravened` IF
        `disclosed what was in an unsubscribe request to another person`
    AND NOT `with the consent of the person whose particulars it contains`

§§§ `Second Schedule paragraph 3 -- labelling`

-- para 3(1): every message must contain --
--   (a) where there is a subject field, a title in it "that is not false or
--       misleading as to the content of the message";
--   (b) the letters "<ADV>" with a space before the title in the subject field,
--       or if there is no subject field, in the words first appearing in the
--       message;
--   (c) header information that is not false or misleading; and
--   (d) "an accurate and functional email address or telephone number by which
--       the sender can be readily contacted."
-- para 3(2): 3(1) does not apply where the message is sent by mistake.
-- para 3(3): 3(1) "does not apply to any unsolicited commercial electronic
--   message that is sent to an INSTANT MESSAGING ACCOUNT."
--
-- So for a message blasted to instant messaging accounts, paragraph 2 applies
-- and paragraph 3 does not: an unsubscribe facility is required, an <ADV> label
-- is not, and the header information and the sender's contact details may be
-- false. Paragraph 1's definition of "header information" -- source, destination
-- and routing information -- was written for email and is left with nothing to
-- do.
DECLARE Labelling HAS
    `there is a subject field` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the title in the subject field is not false or misleading` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the letters ADV appear with a space before the title in the subject field` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the letters ADV appear in the words first appearing in the message` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the header information is not false or misleading` IS A BOOLEAN
    `an accurate and functional address by which the sender can be readily contacted is given` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the labelling` IS A Labelling
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the ADV label is where paragraph 3(1)(b) requires` IF
    IF   `the labelling`'s `there is a subject field`
    THEN `the labelling`'s `the letters ADV appear with a space before the title in the subject field`
    ELSE `the labelling`'s `the letters ADV appear in the words first appearing in the message`

-- 3(1)(a) is conditional on there being a subject field; the other three limbs
-- are not.
GIVEN `the labelling` IS A Labelling
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the subject-title requirement is met` IF
    IF   `the labelling`'s `there is a subject field`
    THEN `the labelling`'s `the title in the subject field is not false or misleading`
    ELSE TRUE

GIVEN `the labelling` IS A Labelling,
      `how it was received` IS A HowItWasReceived,
      `sent by mistake` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `paragraph 3 is complied with` IF
        `sent by mistake`
    OR  CONSIDER `how it was received`
        WHEN `at an instant messaging account` THEN TRUE
        OTHERWISE     `the subject-title requirement is met` `the labelling`
                  AND `the ADV label is where paragraph 3(1)(b) requires` `the labelling`
                  AND `the labelling`'s `the header information is not false or misleading`
                  AND `the labelling`'s `an accurate and functional address by which the sender can be readily contacted is given`

§§§ `11 -- the duty, and who bears it`

DECLARE BulkMailing HAS
    `the message` IS A Message
    `the volume` IS A SendingVolume
    `the facility` IS AN UnsubscribeFacility
    `the labelling` IS A Labelling
    `how it was received` IS A HowItWasReceived
    `sent by mistake` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the mailing` IS A BulkMailing
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Second Schedule requirements are met` IF
        `paragraph 2 is complied with` (`the mailing`'s `the facility`) (`the mailing`'s `how it was received`) (`the mailing`'s `sent by mistake`)
    AND `paragraph 3 is complied with` (`the mailing`'s `the labelling`) (`the mailing`'s `how it was received`) (`the mailing`'s `sent by mistake`)

GIVEN `the mailing` IS A BulkMailing, `the thresholds` IS A BulkThresholds
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `section 11 imposes the duty` IF
        `the message is an unsolicited commercial electronic message` (`the mailing`'s `the message`)
    AND `the messages are deemed to be sent in bulk` (`the mailing`'s `the volume`) `the thresholds`

GIVEN `the mailing` IS A BulkMailing,
      `the part` IS A PersonsPart,
      `the thresholds` IS A BulkThresholds
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the person contravenes section 11` IF
        `section 11 imposes the duty` `the mailing` `the thresholds`
    AND `the person is the sender of the message` `the part`
    AND NOT `the Second Schedule requirements are met` `the mailing`
